WEBVTT

00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:18.330
Concrete Revolutio
 ~Superhuman Phantasmagoria~

00:00:21.540 --> 00:00:25.910
I heard it
 A voice cursing fate

00:00:26.750 --> 00:00:30.080
I found it
 A way to use my power

00:00:30.330 --> 00:00:33.970
What you want are not words,
 are they?

00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:37.290
That love inside
 I want to send it on

00:00:37.930 --> 00:00:40.060
Justice is not on my side

00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:44.410
The only thing absolute for me
 is myself

00:00:45.370 --> 00:00:46.980
Come on Wakers. Ready, go!

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:51.910
Protecting the illusions
 that somebody dreamed of

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:56.450
will liberate the stagnant sky

00:00:56.910 --> 00:01:02.080
We hurl our unanswerable cries
 at each other

00:01:02.370 --> 00:01:06.910
And they become the reason we live

00:01:07.660 --> 00:01:12.580
What can I do in this
 hopeless world we live in?

00:01:13.080 --> 00:01:17.660
Only those that keep searching

00:01:18.140 --> 00:01:20.500
can become the future

00:01:20.660 --> 00:01:24.500
Start the revolution!

00:01:29.940 --> 00:01:32.950
(December, the 16th of Shinka Era,
 Hawaii)

00:01:56.410 --> 00:01:57.330
Fire!

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:02.500
Cease fire.

00:02:13.160 --> 00:02:14.700
He's still alive.

00:02:19.160 --> 00:02:23.950
The most popular theory about
 the beginning of life is this.

00:02:24.160 --> 00:02:28.000
Diverse elements melted into
 the ocean over time.

00:02:28.040 --> 00:02:30.750
By chance, they formed protein,

00:02:30.790 --> 00:02:33.410
and the ocean became
 a primordial soup.

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:35.920
Without this miraculous coincidence,

00:02:36.330 --> 00:02:40.790
life still wouldn't have formed here
 after 4.5 billion years.

00:02:41.450 --> 00:02:42.660
(All lies
 Stupid teacher)

00:02:42.700 --> 00:02:43.700
Morino.

00:02:45.700 --> 00:02:48.060
Oh, am I really that stupid?

00:02:49.250 --> 00:02:51.000
No, I'm the stupid one.

00:02:51.040 --> 00:02:52.060
Teacher!

00:02:52.060 --> 00:02:54.320
When was life formed?

00:02:54.700 --> 00:02:57.750
Well, that's still being researched.

00:02:58.370 --> 00:02:59.450
Your name is...?

00:03:00.040 --> 00:03:01.830
My name is, um...

00:03:01.870 --> 00:03:03.750
That's still being researched.

00:03:03.790 --> 00:03:04.700
What was that?

00:03:04.750 --> 00:03:06.410
He's gone! It's a ghost.

00:03:06.540 --> 00:03:07.790
Correct.

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:11.450
- A cockroach.
 - No, wait, stop.

00:03:11.580 --> 00:03:12.960
No violence.

00:03:19.910 --> 00:03:21.220
Hey, Wakaba.

00:03:21.700 --> 00:03:23.850
Wakaba. She's my type.

00:03:24.200 --> 00:03:26.620
You did it again, didn't you Big Bro?

00:03:27.330 --> 00:03:30.200
Your always frown your lips
 when you mess up.

00:03:30.250 --> 00:03:32.400
I couldn't listen to it anymore.

00:03:32.790 --> 00:03:36.750
Life was born with Earth,
 but he said it was a coincidence.

00:03:36.910 --> 00:03:41.040
Dad always says to dismiss
 what ignorant humans say.

00:03:41.750 --> 00:03:43.620
Don't move.

00:03:44.540 --> 00:03:46.200
Just don't move.

00:03:48.870 --> 00:03:50.830
This is rare for this season.

00:03:50.910 --> 00:03:53.170
Help, Kikko. I know you're there.

00:03:53.870 --> 00:03:56.290
No, I'm not here.

00:03:56.290 --> 00:03:59.510
You meanie!

00:04:00.410 --> 00:04:01.380
We're home.

00:04:01.540 --> 00:04:03.000
Welcome back.

00:04:03.040 --> 00:04:04.700
Hi, Mr. Hitoyoshi.

00:04:04.750 --> 00:04:05.750
Hello.

00:04:05.790 --> 00:04:07.660
- Botchy shogi again?
 - Hey!

00:04:07.700 --> 00:04:10.180
You won't find a husband
 talking like that.

00:04:10.660 --> 00:04:13.350
I've got all the boys to choose from.

00:04:13.580 --> 00:04:17.080
Wakaba will be the prettiest girl
 in the neighborhood.

00:04:17.290 --> 00:04:19.120
You're so lucky.

00:04:19.250 --> 00:04:21.610
She'll be a beauty in a few years.

00:04:21.950 --> 00:04:23.500
We're home.

00:04:23.540 --> 00:04:24.620
Hello dears.

00:04:24.660 --> 00:04:26.620
Here, Megumi. A little gift

00:04:27.620 --> 00:04:28.870
See?

00:04:29.790 --> 00:04:33.250
Such soft hands. I'm in bliss.

00:04:33.620 --> 00:04:36.500
No calls today either, Big Sis?

00:04:37.450 --> 00:04:40.450
Big Bro must be caught somewhere.

00:04:40.540 --> 00:04:41.870
- Poor him.
 - Can't breathe.

00:04:41.910 --> 00:04:43.000
You're right.

00:04:43.040 --> 00:04:48.120
Or else he would've noticed
 the signal 2 years ago.

00:04:48.450 --> 00:04:49.910
(September, the 44th of Shinka Era,
 Setagaya)

00:04:49.950 --> 00:04:50.910
(September, the 43rd of Shinka Era,
 Setagaya)

00:04:50.950 --> 00:04:52.200
(September, the 42nd of Shinka Era,
 Setagaya)

00:04:52.250 --> 00:04:54.120
(October, the 42nd of Shinka Era
 Kawasaki)

00:04:56.500 --> 00:04:57.830
Today at 4 p.m.,

00:04:57.980 --> 00:05:00.610
an ether factory in Kawasaki exploded.

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:04.410
A part of a distilling tank
 burst through the roof.

00:05:04.450 --> 00:05:05.860
It fell on a nearby house.

00:05:05.860 --> 00:05:08.250
A pity for the neighborhood.

00:05:08.290 --> 00:05:10.830
Right when school children go home.

00:05:10.870 --> 00:05:12.620
No hope for survivors.

00:05:13.160 --> 00:05:16.330
It could be an experiment by
 an evil organization.

00:05:16.370 --> 00:05:18.330
There's some strange stories.

00:05:18.450 --> 00:05:20.380
I sent Jiro over to check.

00:05:26.120 --> 00:05:27.590
Health and Welfare Ministry.

00:05:27.830 --> 00:05:30.250
I heard some strange information.

00:05:30.290 --> 00:05:31.720
The survivors, right?

00:05:32.000 --> 00:05:33.850
They lived through this?

00:05:33.850 --> 00:05:38.410
All 6 family members of the house
 closest to the factory were safe.

00:05:39.830 --> 00:05:41.270
They can walk?

00:05:45.700 --> 00:05:46.610
Laughter?

00:05:55.790 --> 00:05:57.410
Hey, stop!

00:05:57.450 --> 00:05:58.370
Stop!

00:05:59.040 --> 00:06:01.090
Then who drove it?

00:06:01.790 --> 00:06:04.830
Somebody in the family
 must've been driving.

00:06:05.410 --> 00:06:08.870
So you're thinking that the family
 might be superhumans.

00:06:09.250 --> 00:06:10.830
It's the morning news.

00:06:11.410 --> 00:06:16.080
An ambulance ran away with a family
 from the Kawasaki ether factory.

00:06:16.450 --> 00:06:18.750
It was found at Tanzawa Canyon.

00:06:19.250 --> 00:06:22.910
It's wrecked
 but no signs of survivors or deaths.

00:06:23.080 --> 00:06:27.410
We still do not know whether
 the 6 mysterious runaways are alive.

00:06:27.450 --> 00:06:28.910
Guess we're right.

00:06:28.950 --> 00:06:32.990
Burned and charred but still alive.
 They must be superhumans.

00:06:33.580 --> 00:06:34.700
I don't get it.

00:06:34.750 --> 00:06:37.410
You don't think they're superhumans?

00:06:37.540 --> 00:06:42.580
I mean, if they're superhumans,
 why stand out so much?

00:06:42.700 --> 00:06:44.000
Chief, what do you think?

00:06:44.410 --> 00:06:47.040
I see. You've got a point.

00:06:47.160 --> 00:06:51.160
Being open about superhumans
 will bring attention.

00:06:51.290 --> 00:06:53.220
They should know that.

00:06:53.500 --> 00:06:56.200
But they still advertised themselves.

00:06:56.450 --> 00:06:57.370
Why?

00:06:57.410 --> 00:06:59.370
A big sale on superhumans.

00:06:59.410 --> 00:07:01.480
Half a dozen including the baby.

00:07:01.660 --> 00:07:03.250
The numbers don't match.

00:07:03.370 --> 00:07:06.000
Do you have someone in mind?

00:07:06.040 --> 00:07:07.990
Well, sort of.

00:07:08.410 --> 00:07:12.910
But the people I know of
 were a group of seven.

00:07:20.450 --> 00:07:24.130
For a long while,
 I'd drifted through the time flow.

00:07:24.450 --> 00:07:27.870
And I saw the same family
 over and over again.

00:07:29.080 --> 00:07:32.290
But I cannot speak about it.

00:07:32.330 --> 00:07:35.000
I see. So there's one missing.

00:07:35.200 --> 00:07:38.890
If it's the same superhuman family
 that Mr. Jaguar knows.

00:07:39.750 --> 00:07:42.370
What I saw was ages ago.

00:07:42.410 --> 00:07:44.650
Yeah, there should be one more.

00:07:45.160 --> 00:07:48.280
Think about it.
 Where's the baby's father?

00:07:49.870 --> 00:07:50.950
Oh my.

00:07:51.000 --> 00:07:54.950
So you know how babies are made.

00:07:55.910 --> 00:07:58.290
I never taught you that.

00:07:58.750 --> 00:08:01.750
The six sent a signal
 to the missing superhuman.

00:08:01.790 --> 00:08:05.410
They might've been separated
 by wars or disasters.

00:08:05.580 --> 00:08:09.040
There's a rumor that
 drifted in from the U.S.

00:08:09.080 --> 00:08:10.620
Where was it again?

00:08:10.910 --> 00:08:13.550
They have something like
 a Superhuman Bureau too.

00:08:14.250 --> 00:08:17.540
We'd promised to
 closely share information,

00:08:17.580 --> 00:08:20.410
but they always
 leave out what's important.

00:08:20.450 --> 00:08:21.850
Here it is.

00:08:23.290 --> 00:08:27.610
They asked about immortal superhumans
 that might exist in Japan.

00:08:28.330 --> 00:08:29.330
Immortal?

00:08:30.660 --> 00:08:34.250
Yes, I remember that incident.
 It was 2 years ago.

00:08:34.580 --> 00:08:37.370
That family was never found.

00:08:37.410 --> 00:08:40.200
I've never heard of that incident.

00:08:40.250 --> 00:08:44.620
2 years ago in the fall.
 You were with that novelty band.

00:08:45.330 --> 00:08:50.380
But to answer us after 2 years?
 The U.S. sure is laid back.

00:08:50.790 --> 00:08:53.630
The papers were held up because
 of Chief Akita.

00:08:54.120 --> 00:08:56.790
Master Ultima finally confessed.

00:08:56.830 --> 00:09:00.330
They've been keeping
 an immortal Japanese superhuman.

00:09:00.540 --> 00:09:01.640
Since when?

00:09:02.580 --> 00:09:04.890
December, the 16th of Shinka Era.

00:09:06.080 --> 00:09:07.900
You mean, since the war?

00:09:08.870 --> 00:09:11.400
He was the first Japanese hostage.

00:09:20.700 --> 00:09:23.410
- How cruel.
 - Living-body experiments?

00:09:23.660 --> 00:09:26.540
They even used militant ants.

00:09:26.700 --> 00:09:28.120
Militant ants?

00:09:28.160 --> 00:09:30.290
Extremely savage ants.

00:09:31.580 --> 00:09:35.700
The ranks of ants that move at 1 kph
 can go up to 20 meters.

00:09:36.160 --> 00:09:39.160
They tried to guide the ants
 with special pheromones

00:09:39.200 --> 00:09:41.580
and use them as
 anti-personnel weapons.

00:09:41.810 --> 00:09:44.290
He was used for that test.

00:09:52.700 --> 00:09:55.910
But they still couldn't reveal
 the key to immortality.

00:09:56.040 --> 00:09:58.200
They've lost purpose for him.

00:09:58.500 --> 00:10:03.330
That's when they got info about
 the family left in Japan.

00:10:03.620 --> 00:10:06.330
So they finally
 confessed his existence.

00:10:06.660 --> 00:10:09.830
Of course,
 we hid the family's whereabouts.

00:10:10.160 --> 00:10:14.750
In truth, we'd found out where
 they'd been hiding a long time ago.

00:10:15.080 --> 00:10:18.220
We knew even the family structure.
 It was easy.

00:10:18.580 --> 00:10:22.970
They're chased down by Japan and
 the U.S. just because they don't die.

00:10:23.500 --> 00:10:26.950
They even have a baby. Poor things.

00:10:27.120 --> 00:10:30.480
But that baby
 might be a few hundred years old.

00:10:31.120 --> 00:10:35.330
Does the U.S. want to carry out
 joint experiments with us?

00:10:35.450 --> 00:10:38.490
They said they'd even let
 the superhuman free.

00:10:38.830 --> 00:10:41.500
Megumi will finally
 get to see her daddy.

00:10:41.540 --> 00:10:44.620
When they do,
 they'll be registered in the Bureau.

00:10:44.660 --> 00:10:47.000
They'll have to cooperate
 in experiments.

00:10:47.040 --> 00:10:49.160
That's too cruel.

00:10:49.250 --> 00:10:50.670
I still don't get it.

00:10:51.040 --> 00:10:52.040
About what?

00:10:53.000 --> 00:10:56.040
They'd hid him for almost 30 years.

00:10:56.080 --> 00:10:58.670
Will they let him go so easily?

00:11:00.330 --> 00:11:02.930
Start monitoring the family.

00:11:03.250 --> 00:11:05.290
Don't let them find you out.

00:11:06.160 --> 00:11:07.500
Yes sir.

00:11:16.700 --> 00:11:17.660
Check.

00:11:17.700 --> 00:11:18.660
Wait.

00:11:18.700 --> 00:11:21.950
See that, Megumi? Grandpa's so weak.

00:11:22.000 --> 00:11:25.120
No, Mr. Magotake is too strong.

00:11:25.540 --> 00:11:28.370
Can I hold Megumi?

00:11:32.370 --> 00:11:33.500
Hello.

00:11:35.000 --> 00:11:37.380
You're so cute.

00:11:42.200 --> 00:11:44.200
Fuurouta's finally back.

00:11:44.250 --> 00:11:46.870
You're beat up.

00:11:49.250 --> 00:11:51.890
They talked me into it,
 saying only I could do it.

00:11:51.890 --> 00:11:53.700
So far, so good.

00:11:56.270 --> 00:11:58.280
(Dear...)

00:12:19.620 --> 00:12:21.340
(Arrival of part 1)

00:12:21.340 --> 00:12:22.200
What?

00:12:22.700 --> 00:12:24.090
Sanae, hurry!

00:12:25.620 --> 00:12:28.180
Hello? Is it you? Is it really you?

00:12:28.870 --> 00:12:31.680
This is Minoru Hatakeyama.
 I've come home.

00:12:32.000 --> 00:12:33.940
Oh, Minoru...

00:12:34.450 --> 00:12:35.830
How are you?

00:12:36.080 --> 00:12:37.290
Yes.

00:12:37.330 --> 00:12:39.320
Yes, yes.

00:12:49.120 --> 00:12:53.330
If it were him,
 he'd want to leave them alone.

00:12:56.040 --> 00:12:58.130
(Arrival of part 2)

00:12:58.130 --> 00:12:59.950
I'm so relieved.

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:04.040
We were at our limits.
 The Population Census is next year...

00:13:04.080 --> 00:13:06.080
Save that stuff for when you meet.

00:13:06.120 --> 00:13:08.050
Where are you, Minoru?

00:13:10.160 --> 00:13:11.270
I'm squished.

00:13:11.660 --> 00:13:14.000
I'm not one for tears.

00:13:14.120 --> 00:13:15.330
Let me.

00:13:15.370 --> 00:13:16.660
Hello?

00:13:17.370 --> 00:13:20.400
So we're going to catch them
 when they meet.

00:13:20.700 --> 00:13:23.700
Yeah. Any calls from
 the American side?

00:13:23.750 --> 00:13:25.370
None at all.

00:13:25.410 --> 00:13:28.540
Do you think they're
 going to leave it to us?

00:13:28.620 --> 00:13:31.410
Just in case,
 see what each base is up to.

00:13:31.450 --> 00:13:32.540
Got it.

00:13:34.870 --> 00:13:36.920
(Arrival of part 3)

00:13:42.250 --> 00:13:44.340
Here to get in our way again?

00:13:45.160 --> 00:13:47.720
What's the Bureau
 going to do with them?

00:13:48.450 --> 00:13:52.560
Just what you used to do.
 Catch and register them.

00:13:52.910 --> 00:13:55.980
Not to protect superhumans
 but to use them.

00:13:57.000 --> 00:13:59.350
Are you going to fight us then?

00:13:59.790 --> 00:14:01.410
I just want to protect them.

00:14:01.450 --> 00:14:03.110
Excuse me.

00:14:03.110 --> 00:14:06.620
The postmaster says this isn't a cafe.

00:14:07.290 --> 00:14:08.830
Is this post office closing?

00:14:08.870 --> 00:14:11.330
Not for 30 minutes, but...

00:14:11.370 --> 00:14:12.410
Just until then.

00:14:12.450 --> 00:14:14.000
But, um...

00:14:14.040 --> 00:14:16.330
Fine then. Give me 10 postcards.

00:14:16.370 --> 00:14:19.870
I'll take 20. I'll take my time
 and write them here.

00:14:23.200 --> 00:14:25.160
(Arrival of part 4)

00:14:28.910 --> 00:14:34.450
There are no signs of U.S. superhumans
 landing at Yokota or Tachikawa.

00:14:34.620 --> 00:14:37.290
I thought they'd set
 Minoru Hatakeyama free

00:14:37.330 --> 00:14:40.270
to follow him to his family.

00:14:40.910 --> 00:14:43.700
They might use
 a huge weapon or a robot.

00:14:43.790 --> 00:14:46.040
There isn't any big cargo, either.

00:14:46.080 --> 00:14:48.280
I see. But keep on the lookout.

00:14:48.870 --> 00:14:49.950
Yes sir.

00:14:51.790 --> 00:14:53.080
Hey, Jiro.

00:14:53.120 --> 00:14:55.450
Won't you come back to the Bureau?

00:14:55.540 --> 00:14:57.080
I'm no longer...

00:14:57.120 --> 00:15:00.120
What can you do without the Bureau?

00:15:01.080 --> 00:15:04.750
Superhumans need to be
 protected by us too.

00:15:04.950 --> 00:15:07.920
Excuse me, but it's time to close.

00:15:08.200 --> 00:15:10.880
He's here! Megumi's dad...

00:15:11.200 --> 00:15:12.510
Jiro Senpai?

00:15:12.790 --> 00:15:13.790
I'll go.

00:15:14.510 --> 00:15:16.700
Are you back at the Bureau?

00:15:16.750 --> 00:15:17.980
Hitoyoshi!

00:15:18.370 --> 00:15:19.910
Stay out of this.

00:15:21.000 --> 00:15:22.870
We're in trouble, something's coming.

00:15:22.910 --> 00:15:24.860
- Jiro Hitoyoshi?
 - What's coming?

00:15:25.370 --> 00:15:27.370
It came after Megumi's dad.

00:15:27.410 --> 00:15:28.540
What?

00:15:28.580 --> 00:15:29.790
We're closing...

00:15:29.830 --> 00:15:31.750
- Jiro!
 - Time's up!

00:15:31.910 --> 00:15:33.030
Then stop the clock.

00:15:34.790 --> 00:15:36.410
Please come again.

00:15:36.750 --> 00:15:40.080
Which is more important,
 Jiro Senpai or our job?

00:15:40.120 --> 00:15:41.370
Who cares?

00:15:41.370 --> 00:15:43.000
Get out of here.

00:15:43.250 --> 00:15:45.200
The Superhuman Bureau, right?

00:15:45.290 --> 00:15:47.410
Do you have no hearts?

00:15:47.910 --> 00:15:49.880
It's been 30 years.

00:15:50.620 --> 00:15:55.510
Minoru became a soldier to
 avoid the registry investigation.

00:15:56.700 --> 00:16:00.000
The family was torn apart
 because of the country.

00:16:00.040 --> 00:16:03.150
Does this country not know
 what compassion is?

00:16:03.410 --> 00:16:07.820
But you're superhumans. You should be
 under government supervision.

00:16:07.820 --> 00:16:11.160
Supervise them to
 use them for wars again?

00:16:11.410 --> 00:16:13.910
How did you say you'd use us?

00:16:16.450 --> 00:16:17.780
What's going on?

00:16:21.040 --> 00:16:22.410
It's a robot!

00:16:26.870 --> 00:16:29.580
The U.S. army. How'd they bring that?

00:16:29.870 --> 00:16:32.700
They'd never meant to do
 joint research.

00:16:32.790 --> 00:16:36.890
They'll take the family. I'll use
 the Ministry of Foreign Affairs.

00:16:36.890 --> 00:16:38.950
Jiro was really there?

00:16:39.000 --> 00:16:42.080
Who cares? The Americans though.
 It's ridiculous.

00:16:42.120 --> 00:16:44.200
Let's take them on.

00:16:47.830 --> 00:16:49.320
Meteortail!

00:17:00.120 --> 00:17:01.250
0 points.

00:17:01.250 --> 00:17:02.660
My turn.

00:17:13.370 --> 00:17:15.250
Once more. Ouch.

00:17:16.000 --> 00:17:19.910
Don't. You might be a ghost,
 but you can't fight a robot.

00:17:20.220 --> 00:17:22.220
Leave it to us. You guys run.

00:17:22.410 --> 00:17:24.370
Ouch.

00:17:25.660 --> 00:17:27.480
It's okay now. Thanks.

00:17:31.000 --> 00:17:32.230
If only I had Equus.

00:17:32.660 --> 00:17:34.120
You better run.

00:17:35.120 --> 00:17:36.580
We can't do that.

00:17:36.740 --> 00:17:39.120
We're here to protect you.

00:17:39.870 --> 00:17:41.200
Mr. Jaguar.

00:17:41.370 --> 00:17:43.080
Take them somewhere safe.

00:17:44.620 --> 00:17:45.790
Got it.

00:17:51.450 --> 00:17:54.080
Kikko, buy some time. Please.

00:17:54.120 --> 00:17:55.970
You called me Kikko.

00:17:56.660 --> 00:17:58.000
You too, Fuurouta.

00:18:02.680 --> 00:18:04.270
Now! Get his eyes.

00:18:04.270 --> 00:18:05.890
Leave it to me.

00:18:06.290 --> 00:18:09.150
Watch how brave I am, Wakaba!

00:18:23.250 --> 00:18:24.290
It's Emi.

00:18:26.330 --> 00:18:28.170
Please, Giant Yokai.

00:18:28.370 --> 00:18:31.700
Leave it to me, Princess.

00:18:47.910 --> 00:18:48.890
What's going on?

00:18:49.620 --> 00:18:51.330
A big yokai... Why?

00:18:51.370 --> 00:18:53.440
It's a weapon made by the U.S. Army.

00:18:54.200 --> 00:18:58.450
A Bio-destroyer that dissolves
 molecular bindings of living things.

00:18:59.250 --> 00:19:03.200
Yokais are beings with life too,
 so they're not exempt.

00:19:03.540 --> 00:19:05.790
What do they want with it?

00:19:06.660 --> 00:19:10.290
They'd never planned on taking
 my family and me.

00:19:10.660 --> 00:19:13.830
The tank isn't that big.
 It'll use it up quickly.

00:19:13.870 --> 00:19:16.830
Sadly, as long as there is
 water close by,

00:19:16.910 --> 00:19:19.540
the Bio-destroyer is unlimited.

00:19:19.660 --> 00:19:23.760
Because the robot itself is
 a moving chemical factory.

00:19:25.910 --> 00:19:28.160
It fights while producing.

00:19:28.200 --> 00:19:30.440
That's what kind of monster it is.

00:19:30.750 --> 00:19:32.660
How can we beat it?

00:19:32.870 --> 00:19:35.450
There's probably just one way.

00:19:38.250 --> 00:19:42.790
It's designed to self-destruct
 once its goal is accomplished.

00:19:42.830 --> 00:19:44.830
It couldn't cause this trouble
 otherwise.

00:19:45.080 --> 00:19:46.120
Its goal?

00:19:46.160 --> 00:19:49.160
Of course. To destroy us.

00:19:49.410 --> 00:19:53.330
If they can't reveal our secret,
 they want us gone.

00:19:53.830 --> 00:19:55.370
Even if we're immortal

00:19:55.410 --> 00:19:59.550
they thought destroying our molecules
 would kill us.

00:20:00.620 --> 00:20:03.540
Thank you, Fuurouta. But goodbye.

00:20:04.370 --> 00:20:05.600
But, wait.

00:20:06.000 --> 00:20:07.910
Don't blush.

00:20:07.950 --> 00:20:11.750
I'm a lot older than you think I am.

00:20:19.910 --> 00:20:21.660
Come now.

00:20:21.700 --> 00:20:23.540
You want to kill us, right?

00:20:23.580 --> 00:20:27.790
I don't know much about those
 molecular whatevers.

00:20:27.830 --> 00:20:30.910
But you came
 all the way to Japan to kill us.

00:20:30.950 --> 00:20:32.410
Such hard work.

00:20:49.870 --> 00:20:52.730
We were supposed to protect them.

00:20:55.230 --> 00:20:58.120
(Searching for signs of life)

00:20:58.410 --> 00:20:59.730
(No signs of life)

00:21:11.830 --> 00:21:15.700
The news will just say
 a tanker crashed or something.

00:21:16.620 --> 00:21:19.700
Jiro, we're not mad so come back.

00:21:28.140 --> 00:21:29.260
Jiro Senpai!

00:21:39.870 --> 00:21:42.730
I saw something unbelievable.

00:21:46.620 --> 00:21:49.750
I wonder if they're superhumans too.

00:21:49.830 --> 00:21:52.870
They're far beyond our understanding.

00:21:52.910 --> 00:21:55.710
Do you still say there's
 a need for the Bureau?

00:21:55.870 --> 00:21:59.330
Isn't thinking you can protect
 superhumans being arrogant?

00:21:59.370 --> 00:22:00.410
Wake up.

00:22:00.870 --> 00:22:05.160
You think they don't need
 the nation's, no, any human's help?

00:22:05.200 --> 00:22:08.040
They're beings that have
 surpassed superhumans?

00:22:09.370 --> 00:22:11.660
They cannot hurt anybody.

00:22:12.080 --> 00:22:14.470
But they cannot be hurt, either.

00:22:15.700 --> 00:22:17.830
Beings that have surpassed humans.

00:22:18.410 --> 00:22:22.540
From the start of this Earth
 till its very end...

00:22:22.580 --> 00:22:24.370
they will live.

00:23:56.750 --> 00:23:59.660
Free History Advocate criminals who
 change history with the Time Watch.

00:23:59.700 --> 00:24:03.580
I'm from the future to catch them.

00:24:04.000 --> 00:24:06.960
In the name of justice,
 I'll fix history to what it should be.

00:24:07.540 --> 00:24:10.660
Yes, I am the Time Patrol.
